          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            What may be called
            %em nonabelian differential cohomology
            – in combination of
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/nonabelian+cohomology"} nonabelian cohomology
            and
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differential+cohomology"} differential cohomology
            – is a notion of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/connections+on+infinity-bundles"} connections on higher bundles
            with
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/higher+group"} higher
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/gauge+group"} gauge group
            being a possibly non-
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/abelian+infinity-group"} abelian
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/n-group"} n-group
          %p
            Early motivation was the observation (
            %a{:href => "#SatiSchreiberStasheff12"}> SSS12
            ) that with the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Green-Schwarz+mechanism"} Green-Schwarz mechanism
            imposed, the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/B-field"} B-field
            in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/heterotic+string+theory"} heterotic string theory
            combines with the ordinary non-abelian
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/gauge+field"} gauge field
            into a non-abelian higher connection (a
            = succeed ")," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/twisted+differential+string+structure"} twisted differential string structure
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/C-field"} C-field
            in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ho%C5%99ava-Witten+theory"} Hořava-Witten theory
            (
            %a{:href => "#FSS15"}> FSS15
            ).
          %p
            Later, the desire to more accurately model more of the expected subtle topological properties of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/C-field"} C-field
            (such as the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/shifted+C-field+flux+quantization"} shifted C-field flux quantization
            combined with
            = succeed "-quantization)" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Page+charge"} Page charge
            = succeed "\u201D)" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/schreiber/show/Hypothesis+H"} Hypothesis H
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/flux+quantization"} flux quantized
            in unstable
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differential+Cohomotopy"} differential
            4-
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cohomotopy"}> Cohomotopy
            , hence with
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+type"} homotopy type
            of its higher gauge group being the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/loop+group"} loop
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/infinity-group"}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
              \-group
            of the 4-sphere. This
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/schreiber/show/Hypothesis+H"} Hypothesis H
            turns out to subtly reproduce the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Green-Schwarz+mechanism"} Green-Schwarz mechanism
            in its lift to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ho%C5%99ava-Witten+theory"} Hořava-Witten theory
            (
            %a{:href => "#FSS22"}> FSS22
            ) and also that on
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/M5-branes"} M5-branes
            (
            %a{:href => "#SS20"}> SS20
            ,
            = succeed ")." do
              %a{:href => "string+structure#FSS21"} FSS21
          %p
            Generally, one may understand
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differential+cohomology"} differential
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/nonabelian+cohomology"} nonabelian cohomology
            as modelling
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/flux+quantization"} flux quantized
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/higher+gauge+theory"} higher gauge fields
            (
            %a{:href => "#SS23"}> SS23
            ).
          %p
            For example, also the “Hypothesis K” of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/D-brane+charge+quantization+in+topological+K-theory"} D-brane charge quantization in topological K-theory
            is, at face value, a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/flux+quantization"} flux quantization
            (of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/RR-field"} RR-field
            combined with the
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/B-field"} B-field
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "/schreiber/show/Introduction+to+Hypothesis+H#OverviewLogicOfFluxQuantization"} here
            %em twisted abelian
            namely as
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/twisted+differential+K-theory"} twisted differential K-theory
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/B-field"} B-field
            as a “
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/background+field"}> background field
            ” and considering the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/RR-field"} RR-field
            in its dependence.
          %h2#related_concepts Related concepts
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/nonabelian+cohomology"} nonabelian cohomology
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differential+cohomology"} differential cohomology
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/higher+gauge+theory"} higher gauge theory
          %h2#references References
          %h3#via_higher_cartan_connections_from_adjusted_weil_algebras Via higher Cartan connections from (adjusted) Weil algebras
          %p Early explorative notes:
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Urs+Schreiber"}> Urs Schreiber
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em On nonabelian differential cohomology
              = succeed "." do
                %a{:href => "https://www.math.uni-hamburg.de/home/schreiber/diffcohslides.pdf"} Slides
          %p
            The local structure of
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/L-infinity+algebra+valued+differential+forms"}
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi L
                        %mn ∞
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L_\infty
                \-algebra valued differential forms
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dg-algebra"} dg-algebra
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homomorphisms"} homomorphisms
            out of (“
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjusted+Weil+algebra"}> adjusted
            ”)
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Weil+algebras"} Weil algebras
            in the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/de+Rham+complex"} de Rham complex
            of the base manifold:
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hisham+Sati"}> Hisham Sati
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Urs+Schreiber"} Urs Schreiber
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jim+Stasheff"} Jim Stasheff
              = succeed "," do
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/schreiber/show/L-infinity+algebra+connections"}
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mi L
                            %mn ∞
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L_\infty
                    algebra connections and applications to String- and Chern-Simons n-transport
              = succeed "," do
                %em Quantum Field Theory
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/0801.3480"} doi:0801.3480
              = succeed "]" do
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1007/978-3-7643-8736-5_17"} doi:10.1007/978-3-7643-8736-5_17
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+integration"} Lie integration
            of this local structure to globally possibly nontrivial actual
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/connections+on+infinity-bundles"} connections on higher bundles
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Domenico+Fiorenza"}> Domenico Fiorenza
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Urs+Schreiber"} Urs Schreiber
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jim+Stasheff"} Jim Stasheff
              = succeed "," do
                %em Čech cocycles for differential characteristic classes
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1011.4735"} arXiv:1011.4735
              = succeed "." do
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1007/BF02104916"} doi:10.1007/BF02104916
          %p
            For the application of this construction to modelling the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Green-Schwarz+mechanism"} Green-Schwarz mechanism
            see
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "#HigherGaugeTheoryOfTheGreenSchwarzMechanismReferences"} below
          %h3#via_the_nonabelian_character_map Via the nonabelian character map
          %p
            A more axiomatic formulation of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differential+cohomology"} differential
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/non-abelian+cohomology"} non-abelian cohomology
            (not yet proven to subsume the above construction) in non-abelian generalization of the original
            %a{:href => "differential}cohomology#HopSin"} Hopkins-Singer construction
            of abelian (namely
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Whitehead-generalized+cohomology"} Whitehead-generalized cohomology
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differential+cohomology"} differential cohomology
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Chern-Dold+character+map"} Chern-Dold character map
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Domenico+Fiorenza"}> Domenico Fiorenza
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Urs+Schreiber"} Urs Schreiber
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hisham+Sati"} Hisham Sati
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "/schreiber/files/NonabelianCharacterWS231212.pdf#page=171"} p. 161
              = succeed "," do
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/schreiber/show/The+Character+Map+in+Non-Abelian+Cohomology"} The Character Map in Non-Abelian Cohomology
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1142/13422"} doi:10.1142/13422
          %p
            On how this generally serves to reflect
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/flux+quantization"} flux quantization
            in
            = succeed ":" do
